      "source": [
        "# Customer Churn Prediction\n",
        "\n",
        "## Project Overview\n",
        "\n",
        "The goal of this project is to develop a machine learning model that can identify customers\n",
        "who are at risk of churning, and examine the characteristics most strongly associated with\n",
        "churn.\n",
        "\n",
        "Two classification models, Logistic Regression and Random Forest, are developed and\n",
        "compared using cross-validation. Since failing to identify a customer who is likely to churn\n",
        "may represent a lost retention opportunity, recall for the churn class will be the primary\n",
        "metric for model selection. Precision, F1, and ROC-AUC will also be evaluated to understand\n",
        "trade-offs between models.\n",
        "\n",
        "The champion model is evaluated on a held-out test set, followed by feature importance\n",
        "and churn-rate analysis to translate the model results into potential business insights.\n"
      ]
    },
