    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "59019e26-76eb-48ce-b672-5aefd1f3975c",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Gender and senior-citizen status are examined to understand differences in the churn rates. If included as model inputs , their potential influence on predictions should be considered when interpreting results and making recommendations."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "f78ada9c-c1b3-4448-a8ff-f1e02d27e510",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Relationship Between Charges and Tenure\n",
        "\n",
        "'TotalCharges' reflects charges accumulated over a customer's tenure, so I will compare it with both 'tenure' and 'MonthlyCharges'. These plots will help me decide whether keeping all three variables adds useful information or creates considerable overlap."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 14,
      "id": "581ddec1-adf8-4fec-b1fa-930d50dc8817",
      "metadata": {
        "trusted": true
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
            "image/png": "",
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 1300x500 with 2 Axes>"
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "display_data"
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "#Visualizing tenure and monthly charges against total charges due to expected multicollinearity.\n",
        "fig ,axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(13,5))\n",
        "\n",
        "axes[0].scatter(data['tenure'],\n",
        "                data['TotalCharges'],\n",
        "                alpha = 0.4\n",
        "               )\n",
        "\n",
        "axes[0].set_title('Tenure vs. TotalCharges')\n",
        "axes[0].set_xlabel('Tenure')\n",
        "axes[0].set_ylabel('Total Charges')\n",
        "\n",
        "axes[1].scatter(data['MonthlyCharges'],\n",
        "                data['TotalCharges'],\n",
        "                alpha = 0.4\n",
        "               )\n",
        "\n",
        "axes[1].set_title('Monthly vs Total Charges')\n",
        "axes[1].set_xlabel('Monthly Charges')\n",
        "axes[1].set_ylabel('Total Charges')\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "18b71a9c-11fc-4750-b4da-5458d28e36d0",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Total charges generally increased with both tenure and monthly charges. Because it represents accumulated charges, it has overlapping info with both features. It will be dropped to reduce redundancy among the predictors.\n",
        "\n",
        "I will also drop the CustomerID column since it is sensitive information and has no predictive value."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 15,
      "id": "bc5fe4e5-1d8f-4b96-a319-46f4d645bbf5",
      "metadata": {
        "trusted": true
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "data = data.drop(columns=['customerID','TotalCharges'])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "f4e287f0-9284-4271-8b13-8ebeada36059",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Train/Test Split\n",
        "\n",
        "I reserved 30% of the data as a hold-out set for final testing. Stratifying by 'Churn' keeps the churn proportion similar in the training and test sets."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 16,
      "id": "a3edbb93-63bd-4916-a991-9f661ec566d4",
      "metadata": {
        "trusted": true
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "X = data.drop(columns='Churn')\n",
        "y = data['Churn']\n",
        "\n",
        "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(X, y, test_size=0.3, stratify=y, random_state=42)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "b6798163-7c67-46d7-967a-9041d61da806",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Preprocessing Pipeline\n",
        "\n",
        "Numeric features are standardized and categorical features one-hot encoded. No imputation is needed since there are no missing values. Keeping these steps in a pipeline ensures that preprocessing is learned from the training data during model fitting."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 17,
      "id": "6304106f-f195-4c45-910e-8cb854a828a1",
      "metadata": {
        "trusted": true
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "numerical_cols = X.select_dtypes(include='number').columns.to_list()\n",
        "categorical_cols = X.select_dtypes(include='str').columns.to_list()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 18,
      "id": "4e87ca66-815a-437d-ae18-853ee2da6ee1",
      "metadata": {
        "trusted": true
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "numerical_pipeline = Pipeline([\n",
        "    ('scalar', StandardScaler())\n",
        "])\n",
        "\n",
        "categorical_pipeline = Pipeline([\n",
        "    ('encoder', OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown='ignore'))\n",
        "])\n",
        "\n",
        "preprocessor = ColumnTransformer([\n",
        "    ('num',numerical_pipeline,numerical_cols),\n",
        "    ('cat',categorical_pipeline,categorical_cols)\n",
        "])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "74dfdba8-cddb-4eb6-a9ac-7fb0f0cc36e1",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Logistic Regression\n",
        "\n",
        "I will use logistic regression as a baseline for predicting churn. Because fewer customers churned than stayed, I set the class weight as balanced to give errors in the two classes more equal weight during training."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 19,
      "id": "5cf0c4a4-799a-4f51-b7e9-57b5aa33e616",
      "metadata": {
        "trusted": true
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "log_reg_pipeline = Pipeline([\n",
        "    ('preprocessor',preprocessor),\n",
        "    ('classifier',LogisticRegression(\n",
        "        max_iter = 1000,\n",
        "        class_weight='balanced'\n",
        "    ))\n",
        "])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 20,
      "id": "030a75de-05d1-42fd-b102-9a3bcb9cb849",
      "metadata": {
        "trusted": true
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "#Assigning values to cv, scoring, and creating a function to evalute cv results.\n",
        "cv = StratifiedKFold(\n",
        "    n_splits=5,\n",
        "    shuffle=True,\n",
        "    random_state=42)\n",
        "\n",
        "scoring = {\n",
        "    'f1':'f1',\n",
        "    'recall':'recall',\n",
        "    'precision':'precision',\n",
        "    'roc_auc':'roc_auc'\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "def model_scores(model):\n",
        "    for metric in scoring:\n",
        "        scores = model[f'test_{metric}']\n",
        "        print(f'{metric}: {scores.mean():.3f} +/- {scores.std():.3f}')"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 21,
      "id": "dcf9053b-52a9-4afc-b487-632d7840a9de",
      "metadata": {
        "trusted": true
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "f1: 0.625 +/- 0.019\n",
            "recall: 0.794 +/- 0.016\n",
            "precision: 0.515 +/- 0.024\n",
            "roc_auc: 0.842 +/- 0.012\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "log_reg_cv_results = cross_validate(\n",
        "    log_reg_pipeline,\n",
        "    X_train,\n",
        "    y_train,\n",
        "    cv=cv,\n",
        "    scoring=scoring\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "model_scores(log_reg_cv_results)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "5202119b-7414-4c74-a642-bf41909db5b1",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Across five cross-validation folds, the baseline logistic regression model achieved mean recall of 0.794, precision of 0.515, F1 of 0.625, and ROC-AUC of 0.842. Its recall suggests it identified about 79% of customers who churned within the validation folds. Its lower precision means many of the customers flagged as likely to churn did not. These results will be used as a baseline when comparing tuned models."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 22,
      "id": "8d0f6f7d-f74a-403f-8933-4ccf38ccdeb4",
      "metadata": {
        "trusted": true
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Best C:  {'classifier__C': 15}\n",
            "Best CV Recall:  0.7958556345237051\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "#Logistic regression hyperparameter tuning.\n",
        "log_reg_param_grid = {'classifier__C': [0.01,0.1,1,5,10,15,100]}\n",
        "\n",
        "log_reg_grid = GridSearchCV(\n",
        "    log_reg_pipeline,\n",
        "    param_grid=log_reg_param_grid,\n",
        "    scoring='recall',\n",
        "    cv=cv,\n",
        "    n_jobs=-1\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "log_reg_grid.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
        "\n",
        "print('Best C: ',log_reg_grid.best_params_)\n",
        "print('Best CV Recall: ',log_reg_grid.best_score_)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 23,
      "id": "a3652fb3-50ee-4ba9-a87f-fffcf451dba0",
      "metadata": {
        "trusted": true
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "f1: 0.624 +/- 0.019\n",
            "recall: 0.796 +/- 0.017\n",
            "precision: 0.513 +/- 0.023\n",
            "roc_auc: 0.842 +/- 0.012\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "#Logistic regression final tuned model cv results.\n",
        "final_log_reg = log_reg_grid.best_estimator_\n",
        "\n",
        "final_log_cv_results = cross_validate(\n",
        "    final_log_reg,\n",
        "    X_train,\n",
        "    y_train,\n",
        "    cv=cv,\n",
        "    scoring=scoring\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "model_scores(final_log_cv_results)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "8c676f57-4715-4d30-b976-772601a84ec1",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Logistic Regression Tuning Results\n",
        "\n",
        "Grid search selected C=15 using recall as the selection metric. The tuned model's cross-validation recall was about 0.796, which is nearly identical to the baseline. All other metrics decreased slightly. Tuning did not result in any noticeable improvement to the model."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "5cd4cec0-9c09-4d2e-a810-4d3992cdac96",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Random Forest"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 24,
      "id": "8c46efd0-68b6-4aa8-abd3-118ac298b61a",
      "metadata": {
        "trusted": true
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "rf_pipeline = Pipeline([\n",
        "    ('preprocessor',preprocessor),\n",
        "    ('classifier',RandomForestClassifier(random_state=42))\n",
        "])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 25,
      "id": "ad74414e-9ce2-4cca-aed6-355df85efb17",
      "metadata": {
        "trusted": true
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "f1: 0.552 +/- 0.018\n",
            "recall: 0.495 +/- 0.020\n",
            "precision: 0.624 +/- 0.018\n",
            "roc_auc: 0.816 +/- 0.013\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "rf_cv_results = cross_validate(\n",
        "    rf_pipeline,\n",
        "    X_train,\n",
        "    y_train,\n",
        "    cv=cv,\n",
        "    scoring=scoring\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "model_scores(rf_cv_results)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "0216bcfe-c037-487a-83a5-385fe42039ee",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Across five cross-validation folds, the baseline random forest model achieved mean recall of 0.495, precision of 0.624, F1 of 0.552, and ROC-AUC of 0.816. Its recall suggests it identified about 50% of customers who churned within the validation folds. Its higher precision compared to the logistic regression model means less customers were incorrectly flagged to churn."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 26,
      "id": "3ca80e00-9358-4350-96e7-1b9d0bdf1c6f",
      "metadata": {
        "trusted": true
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Best params:  {'classifier__class_weight': 'balanced', 'classifier__max_depth': None, 'classifier__max_features': 'sqrt', 'classifier__min_samples_leaf': 20, 'classifier__min_samples_split': 2, 'classifier__n_estimators': 400}\n",
            "Best CV Recall:  0.8012108449591999\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "#Random forest hyperparameter tuning.\n",
        "rf_param_grid = {\n",
        "    'classifier__n_estimators': [300,400,500],\n",
        "    'classifier__max_depth': [10,None],\n",
        "    'classifier__min_samples_split': [2,4],\n",
        "    'classifier__min_samples_leaf': [1,5,10,20],\n",
        "    'classifier__max_features': ['sqrt'],\n",
        "    'classifier__class_weight': ['balanced']\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "rf_grid = GridSearchCV(\n",
        "    rf_pipeline,\n",
        "    param_grid=rf_param_grid,\n",
        "    scoring='recall',\n",
        "    cv=cv,\n",
        "    n_jobs=-1\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "rf_grid.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
        "\n",
        "print('Best params: ',rf_grid.best_params_)\n",
        "print('Best CV Recall: ',rf_grid.best_score_)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "8bc0f77c-50d6-49c2-91b8-85fedaebb455",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Random Forest Tuning Results\n",
        "\n",
        "I tuned the random forest using recall as the grid-search scoring metric. The best settings increased cross-validation recall significantly compared with the untuned model. I will now evaluate the remaining metrics for the tuned model so I can compare it with logistic regression on more than one measure."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
